# Find Project Simplifications

Look for duplicated ownership, redundant layers, unused configuration, parallel implementations, unnecessary abstractions, and documentation that repeats source. Propose only changes that reduce total concepts or maintenance cost. Identify the preserved behavior and validation evidence. Do not call a deletion a simplification when it moves complexity elsewhere or weakens an established contract.
